  "codex_last_message": "Changed this cycle: I tested two Rust no-tail request-cache variants in `src/db.rs`, but neither produced a durable win, so I restored the proven cycle-5 hot path. The kept changes are harness/docs only: [.meta_codex/tools/analyze_request_cache_keys](</__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/tools/analyze_request_cache_keys:1>) now reports `direct_safe`, and I recorded the outcome in [.meta_codex/research_notes.md](</__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/research_notes.md:1>) and [.meta_codex/campaign_journal.md](</__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/.meta_codex/campaign_journal.md:1>). `src/db.rs` now matches the mainline snapshot again, and `build_project` passed.\n\nScore expectation is unchanged from the incumbent branch. Best valid full remains `11126.51 QPS` at `1.0000` recall from cycle 5, and the honest expectation is still roughly low-10k full / low-12k quick. The cycle-6 no-tail experiments were valid but not convincing: clean quick samples came in at `11563.87`, `10149.57`, and `10369.97 QPS`, so I did not keep them and I did not spend a full benchmark on the reverted state.\n\nNext best move: stop treating tail verification as the main bottleneck. The strongest next branch is to capture the exact reqwest wire shape and cut request parsing / transport overhead in [src/server.rs](</__modal/volumes/vo-WauxZXgTehLrBgTwgcOh2J/campaign/workspace/src/server.rs:1>), or build a stronger exact request classifier that reduces key construction work instead of only removing the final verification step.",
